\chapter{Structural Invariant Computation in the Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE)}
\section{Overview}

Chapter 5 formalizes the computation of structural invariants within the Temporal
Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE). Structural invariants are the conserved quantities,
manifold constraints, and temporal symmetry-preserving metrics that define the
admissible evolution of TSSE-governed systems. These invariants ensure that
relativistic propulsion, fusion energetics, and temporal symmetry kernels evolve
within closed, stable, and mathematically rigorous manifolds.

This chapter establishes:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item The definition and classification of TSSE structural invariants.
  \item The invariant computation operators and their algebraic properties.
  \item The Hamiltonian and symplectic derivation of invariants.
  \item The manifold-preserving theorems governing invariant evolution.
  \item The canonical TSSE Structural Invariant Kernel (TSSE-SIK).
\end{enumerate}

