\section{Classification of TSSE Structural Invariants}

TSSE structural invariants fall into three primary classes:
\[
\mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left\{
\mathcal{I}_{\text{T}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{R}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{F}}
\right\},
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $\mathcal{I}_{\text{T}}$ are temporal invariants.
  \item $\mathcal{I}_{\text{R}}$ are relativistic propulsion invariants.
  \item $\mathcal{I}_{\text{F}}$ are fusion energetic invariants.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Temporal Invariants}

Temporal invariants satisfy:
\[
\mathcal{T}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{T}.
\]

\subsection{Relativistic Invariants}

Relativistic invariants satisfy:
\[
\det(D\mathcal{U}(t)) = 1,
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J.
\]

\subsection{Fusion Invariants}

Fusion invariants satisfy:
\[
G(q,p) = \frac{E_{\text{fusion}}}{E_{\text{ann}}} = Q.
\]

These invariants define the admissible class of TSSE-governed systems.

