\section{Invariant Computation Operators}

Define the invariant computation operator:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}} : (q,p) \mapsto \mathcal{I}(q,p),
\]
where $\mathcal{I}$ is any TSSE structural invariant.

\begin{definition}[Invariant Operator]
An invariant operator $\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}$ satisfies:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p)) = \mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(q,p).
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Operator Commutation]
Invariant operators commute with TSSE evolution:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since invariants are preserved under TSSE evolution, applying $\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}$
before or after $\mathcal{U}(t)$ yields identical results.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the algebraic consistency of invariant computation.

