\section{Manifold-Preserving Theorems}

Let $\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}$ denote the global structural manifold.

\begin{theorem}[Invariant Manifold Closure]
If $(q,p) \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}$, then:
\[
\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p) \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}.
\]
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Follows from the closure of subsystem manifolds and the direct product structure
of $\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}}$.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Invariant Preservation Under Symplectic Flow]
If $\mathcal{U}(t)$ is symplectic, then all TSSE invariants are preserved:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p)) = \mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(q,p).
\]
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Symplectic evolution preserves Hamiltonian invariants, manifold constraints, and
temporal symmetry operators.
\end{proof}

These theorems establish the global stability of TSSE engines.

