\section{Canonical TSSE Structural Invariant Kernel (TSSE-SIK)}

The TSSE Structural Invariant Kernel is defined by:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-SIK}} =
\left(
\mathcal{I}_{\text{T}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{R}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{F}},\;
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}},\;
\mathcal{U}(t)
\right).
\]

It enforces:
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p)) = \mathcal{C}_{\mathcal{I}}(q,p),
\qquad
\mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}} = \mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE}},
\qquad
\det(D\mathcal{U}(t)) = 1.
\]

This kernel defines the invariant computation layer of TSSE engines.

